\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>This evening's </strong>random act of kindness — times two — happened more than 50 years ago. But it has stayed with the recipient, Peggy Elmhorst of New Orleans, ever since:</p><ul><li><strong>\"I was on a very tight budget, </strong>in the grocery, picking and choosing what would see me through for two weeks, when the next paycheck would appear.\"</li><li><strong>\"As I was checking out,</strong> I realized I had somehow lost my cash. I asked the clerk if I could go look for it on the floor, but the manager had it. Some kind soul had found it and turned it in. I was feeling so thankful that I would be able to pay for my purchases, when I was told by the clerk that the person originally behind me in line had paid for my food.\"</li><li><strong>\"Two kindnesses!</strong> I was 23 years old. Today, I'm 80 and have never forgotten how much kindness can change situations for people. I have tried to be worthy by passing it on.\"</li></ul><p>📮<em> Share the bits of goodness you've witnessed in the world — along with your name and hometown — with <a href=\"mailto:finishline@axios.com\" target=\"_blank\">finishline@axios.com</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48499577.262234/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtNzIxYjhlMjAtMDc5OS00M2EwLTgwMTktNzc1OGYyOGZhNjVmLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QyJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkyJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXd